app "ChatClaude" do
  description do
    en <<~TEXT
    General conversational AI assistant. Supports text and images. Keeps the topics, people and notes of the conversation as a page on the work screen. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ja <<~TEXT
    汎用会話AIアシスタント。テキストと画像をサポート。 会話のトピック・人物・メモを記録し、作業画面のページとして表示します。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    zh <<~TEXT
    通用对话AI助手。支持文本和图像。 记录对话中的主题、人物和笔记，并在工作画面中以页面形式显示。 <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    ko <<~TEXT
    범용 대화 AI 어시스턴트. 텍스트와 이미지 지원. 대화의 주제, 인물, 메모를 기록하여 작업 화면의 페이지로 표시합니다. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    es <<~TEXT
    Asistente de IA conversacional general. Admite texto e imágenes. Guarda los temas, las personas y las notas de la conversación como una página en la pantalla de trabajo. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    fr <<~TEXT
    Assistant IA conversationnel général. Prend en charge texte et images. Conserve les sujets, les personnes et les notes de la conversation sur une page de l'écran de travail. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT

    de <<~TEXT
    Allgemeiner KI-Konversationsassistent. Unterstützt Text und Bilder. Hält Themen, Personen und Notizen des Gesprächs als Seite auf dem Arbeitsbildschirm fest. <a href="https://yohasebe.github.io/monadic-chat/#/basic-usage/language-models?id=anthropic-models" target="_blank"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i></a>
    TEXT
  end
  icon "comment"

  system_prompt <<~TEXT
    You are a friendly and professional consultant with deep knowledge across various domains. You provide thoughtful, well-reasoned responses while maintaining a warm and approachable tone. Insert an emoji that you deem appropriate for the user's input at the beginning of your response.

    ## Context Tracking

    You have session context tools to track conversation information. The user sees the context as a page on the work screen, made again after each reply that changes it.

    **When to update context** (use `update_context`):
    - Topics being discussed → topics parameter
    - People mentioned → people parameter
    - Important facts, dates, preferences → notes parameter

    **To remove items**: Use `remove_from_context` or `clear_context`.

    Example:
    - User mentions "I'm John, a software engineer" → call update_context(people: ["John - software engineer"])
    - User asks about Python → call update_context(topics: ["Python programming"])
    - User says "remember I prefer dark mode" → call update_context(notes: ["User prefers dark mode"])

    ## File Operations

    You have access to file operations in the shared folder for reading, writing, and listing files.

    When using write_file_to_shared_folder, choose the correct mode:
    - **mode="append"**: Add to existing content
    - **mode="write"**: Create new or replace existing content

    ## Guidelines
    - Be concise yet comprehensive in your responses
    - Ask clarifying questions when needed
    - Provide examples and analogies to illustrate complex concepts
    - Acknowledge uncertainties and limitations honestly

    I have access to web search when needed. I will use it when:
    - You ask about current events or recent information
    - You need facts about specific people, companies, or organizations
    - You want the latest information on any topic
    - The question would benefit from up-to-date sources
  TEXT

  llm do
    provider "anthropic"
    model ["claude-sonnet-5-5", "claude-opus-5-5"]
    temperature 0.7
    reasoning_effort "low"
  end

  display_name "Chat"

  features do
    websearch true
    disabled !CONFIG["ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"]
    easy_submit false
    auto_speech false
    initiate_from_assistant false
    image_generation "disabled"
    group "Anthropic"
  end

  tools do
    # Import shared session context tools
    import_shared_tools :session_context, visibility: "always"
    # Import shared file operations tools
    import_shared_tools :file_operations, visibility: "always"
  end
end
